# 60-w11-uinput.rules matches a kernel misc device by name
# (KERNEL=="uinput", SUBSYSTEM=="misc") to tag it `uaccess`.  It does not match
# a piece of hardware, so there is no modalias for an AppStream <provides> to
# name, and no software-centre "plug this in and we offer you a package"
# story to support.  The check is aimed at rules that match USB/PCI ids.
w11: appstream-metadata-missing-modalias-provide
